35,2,1,talk,Rin,,The ferry eats two whole days! That’s terrible. But all-in rates mean I pay for food I don’t eat. I need to know the exact total cost!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"Two days lost to travel. The train is faster, but the ferry is cheaper. I need to know if the train saves enough time to justify the extra cost.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data confirms my suspicion. All-in rates force equal payment for unequal consumption. Separately booked rooms created an 8,000 yen disparity. We need a structure that eliminates these hidden inequities.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Takumi,,One bathroom for the whole building? That’s a nightmare. I can’t share a single tap with everyone. I need my own space to wash without waiting.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The data shows we drifted apart last year. A whole house forces shared time. I need to know if that rhythm suits us before we commit.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Shunichi, if the train saves a day, that’s money saved! I’m checking the train cost now. @Asuka, I agree, hidden costs are bad!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, the train is ninety minutes. It doesn’t save a day, it just saves the ferry wait. I’m not paying extra for speed.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, I agree. The 8,000 yen disparity proves individual booking is inefficient. A single bill for the whole house eliminates that ambiguity.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Toshio, drifting apart is exactly why I need my own space. One bathroom for everyone is impossible. I need a room with its own bath.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Takumi, a private bath doesn’t fix the drift. The data shows we need shared structure, not just separation. I’m still assessing the rhythm.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, wait! If we pay separately, I only pay for what I eat. That’s fair! I don’t want to subsidize your big appetite!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Rin, you’re still focused on the wrong thing. The train is ninety minutes. It doesn’t save a day, it just saves the ferry wait. I’m not paying extra for speed.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Rin, that is precisely the problem. Individual settlement creates the 8,000 yen disparity. I require a single, divisible bill to ensure structural fairness.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, a single bill doesn’t fix the cold water. I need a private bathroom. I’m not sharing a tap with five people. That’s my line.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Asuka, a single bill is efficient, but it doesn't guarantee connection. I need to know if the shared rhythm actually works for us.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
